From e9245cd990448a4e716b620d5c57f1e003a49334 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashish Kumar Singh <ashishkmr472@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:52:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [PJRT:GPU] The CUDA plugin serves its executables' metadata,
 and the C API client reads their buffer assignment from it

PJRT_Executable_GetCompiledMemoryStats' struct carries no buffer assignment, so a client over the C API read
serialized_buffer_assignment empty from every GPU plugin. The plugin registers PJRT_ExecutableMetadata_Extension,
serving PjRtExecutableMetadata with the executable's compiled memory stats, the assignment among them (a full
compile's or one stopped after buffer assignment), and PjRtCApiExecutable::GetCompiledMemoryStats fills the
assignment from it where the plugin serves the extension.
